ts=2026-04-18T14:49:33.789Z type=pattern scope=codebase:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="In tests under tests/test_indicators/, files commonly use sys.path.insert(...) before first-party imports; Ruff I001 on these files can come from an extra blank line after the import block rather than import ordering, so prefer minimal whitespace-only fixes to avoid broad formatter churn." issue=ENG-33 tags=python,ruff,tests,minimal-fix
ts=2026-04-18T14:55:25.910Z type=pattern scope=codebase:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="Input validators using `np.isfinite(series).all()` can raise `TypeError` if dtype is non-numeric/object; consider coercion or try/except to rethrow `ValueError` for clearer API contract (noted during ENG-33 review in `indicators/structure.py::_validate_ohlcv`)." issue=ENG-33 tags=validation,numpy,pandas,security,edge-case
ts=2026-04-18T15:01:05.700Z type=pattern scope=shion:qa content="When reviewing indicator/regime classifiers, watch for tests that only assert label ∈ allowed set (schema-only) and don't assert expected label/decision_rule per fixture; also verify fixtures actually exercise intended branch (e.g., breakout fixture can yield transition due to no swings/range detection or recency window). Treat as Lane B FAIL/high because regressions pass CI." issue=ENG-33 market structure summary tags=lane-b,qa,tests,edge-cases,fixtures,regression-risk
ts=2026-04-18T16:25:29.940Z type=context scope=codebase:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="ENG-34 backlog structural review: ticket scope is repo-aligned to existing screener ownership surfaces (`src/tempest_mcp/screener/scanner.py`, `src/tempest_mcp/tools/screener_tools.py`, `src/tempest_mcp/server.py`) and explicitly excludes ENG-35/ENG-36/ENG-38. Minor open design clarifications only: ranking/tie-break rules, empty-filter/default-threshold behavior, and deterministic partial-data handling." issue=ENG-34 tags=backlog-review,screener,repo-contract,scope-review
ts=2026-04-18T17:45:26.352Z type=decision scope=shuna:eng-34 content="ENG-34 design constrains implementation to scanner.py (engine), screener_tools.py (tool orchestration), server.py (schema/validation only), and tests. No crypto_screener.py or new endpoint; preserve session_breakout_scan boundary for ENG-35. Screener response must be deterministic, serializable, and include applied_config, ranked results, and per-symbol failures." issue=ENG-34 tags=design,screener,contract,determinism
ts=2026-04-18T17:45:26.380Z type=context scope=codebase:tempest-tradingview-mcp content="Current contract snapshot before ENG-34 implementation: screener_tools.screener_scan is a stub returning success+data.stub=true; server validates screener_scan symbols only (not filters/min_score thresholds); scanner.scan currently computes RSI oversold and EMA values but does not fully evaluate declared multi-factor filter surface." issue=ENG-34 tags=contract,scanner,server,stub,tests
